<title>USA: Bayer raises thermoplastic capacity.</title>
<headline>Bayer raises thermoplastic capacity.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayer Corp said Monday it has completed a $20 million expansion of its Polymers Division Newark compounding plant for the plastics industry at Hebron, Ohio, adding 30 jobs in the local community.</p>
<p>The production capacity was increased by 56 percent, the Bayer AG subsidiary said. The plant now can compound in excess of 80 million pounds of thermoplastics annually following the addition of 45,000 square feet in manufacturing and warehouse space, two extruders, an automated packaging system and a material staging area.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
